        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 14,
        "titulo": "The complete table of articles",
        "explicacao": "This is the table that organises everything. Three shortcuts: (1) the FEMININE and the PLURAL hardly change; they only change in the dative and the genitive. (2) The NEUTER is the same as the nominative in the accusative, and the same as the masculine in the dative and the genitive. (3) In the accusative only the masculine changes. Other details: in the genitive, the masculine and neuter noun gets -s or -es («des Mannes», «des Kindes»); in the dative plural, the noun gets -n («den Kindern»), unless it already ends in -n or -s.",
        "exemplos": [
          {
            "ru": "Der Mann gibt dem Kind einen Apfel.",
            "pt": "The man gives an apple to the child."
          },
          {
            "ru": "Die Frau hilft der Nachbarin.",
            "pt": "A mulher ajuda a vizinha."
          },
          {
            "ru": "Das ist das Auto des Lehrers.",
            "pt": "This is the teacher's car."
          }
